<title>USA: Time Inc names Wallace editor of People-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Time Inc names Wallace editor of People-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc's Time Inc named Carol Wallace managing editor of People, the most profitable magazine in publishing, the Wall Street Journal said in Thursday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>Wallace, previously deputy managing editor of the magazine, replaced Landon Jones Jr who became vice president of strategic planning for Time Inc, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>--New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
